# Copy to .env (or set in your shell / launcher) — do NOT commit the real values.

# Required: absolute path to your Obsidian vault (or any folder of .md files)
VAULT_PATH=/path/to/your/obsidian/vault

# Optional: where to store the SQLite index + embedding cache.
# Defaults to $XDG_DATA_HOME/obsidian-brain or ~/.local/share/obsidian-brain
# DATA_DIR=/path/to/data/dir

# Pick a preset (easiest). Default is "english". Ignored if EMBEDDING_MODEL is set.
# Presets:
#   english         Xenova/bge-small-en-v1.5               34 MB  English (default, asymmetric)
#   english-fast    MongoDB/mdbr-leaf-ir                   22 MB  English, retrieval-tuned, asymmetric (v1.7.4+)
#   english-quality Xenova/bge-base-en-v1.5               110 MB  English, highest CPU quality
#   multilingual    Xenova/multilingual-e5-small          135 MB  94 languages
#   multilingual-openai  Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B  (served by llama.cpp etc., see below)
# Deprecated aliases: fastest → english-fast (now mdbr-leaf-ir), balanced → english (was all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
#EMBEDDING_PRESET=english

# Power-user: specify any transformers.js-compatible or Ollama model id directly.
# Overrides EMBEDDING_PRESET when set.
#EMBEDDING_MODEL=Xenova/bge-base-en-v1.5

# For multilingual without the 118 MB transformers.js tax, use Ollama instead:
#EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama
#EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:0.6b

# Embedding provider — default is "transformers" (local, no setup). Set to
# "ollama" to use a local Ollama server for higher-quality embeddings, or to
# "openai-compatible" for any server speaking POST /v1/embeddings.
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# With EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama, EMBEDDING_MODEL selects the Ollama model
# (default: nomic-embed-text). Pull it first with: ollama pull <model>.
# OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_DIM is optional — if unset the server probes the model
# on startup. Well-known dims:
#   nomic-embed-text      = 768
#   mxbai-embed-large     = 1024
#   bge-large             = 1024
#   qwen3-embedding-8b    = 4096
# OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_DIM=768

# ── OpenAI-compatible provider (llama.cpp, LM Studio, vLLM, TEI, OpenAI) ──
# For any server that speaks `POST /v1/embeddings`. The canonical provider name
# describes the PROTOCOL, not the vendor — nothing leaves your machine unless
# you point EMBEDDING_BASE_URL at a hosted endpoint. These aliases all work:
# openai-compatible, openai, llamacpp, llama.cpp, lmstudio, vllm, tei.
#
# Easiest path — the preset picks Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B and the bundled seed
# supplies its instruction-aware query prefix and 32 768-token context:
#EMBEDDING_PRESET=multilingual-openai
#EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=llamacpp
#EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# Start the server first (note --embedding; --pooling last is required for the
# Qwen3-Embedding family, which pools on the final token rather than the mean):
#   llama-server -m Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf \
#     --embedding --pooling last -c 8192 -ub 8192 --port 8080
#
# Optional — skip the one throwaway probe embed at startup by declaring the dim.
# Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B = 1024, -4B = 2560, -8B = 4096, bge-m3 = 1024.
#EMBEDDING_DIM=1024
#
# Optional — only for servers that require auth. Local llama.cpp does not.
#EMBEDDING_API_KEY=sk-...
